```python
def fib(n, memo={}):
    if n in memo:
        return memo[n]
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    memo[n] = fib(n - 1, memo) + fib(n - 2, memo)
    return memo[n]
```

Time complexity is O(n) because each Fibonacci value is computed only once and stored in the memo dictionary. Space complexity is O(n) due to the memo table storing up
